# Fixed 2026-11-26, defect 2850, lane sig-family (step 199b).
# The third coroutine of a chain of `uc_link`s, on the runner's frame: refused.
# Symptom: before, a handler's jump into a coroutine the C library started
# through another's `uc_link`, on a stack carved from the thread's own, ran the
# Heroes function inside the signal at exit 0, plain on this Mac and on Linux
# arm64 (refused under `--sanitize` on this Mac only by the frame walk); on
# the heap it was refused in words naming causes the program has none of.
# Cause: a range `makecontext` was given is entered only by a switch the
# runtime sees, and the C library's own switch to `uc_link` at a coroutine's
# end is none, so the linked range was judged the thread's own memory.
# Fix: the link is learned where `makecontext` reads it; a range entered holds
# every range down its chain of links entered with it, and their end is seen
# where the swap into the first returns, each whose context still names what
# it named when the swap began and from which no switch was made.
extern "fixedbugs-2850-coroutines-the-c-library-starts-through-uc-link.h"
    function ul_run(form: i32, cb: (function(i64) -> i64)) -> i64
    function ul_reuse(cb: (function(i64) -> i64)) -> i64

function answer(n: i64) -> i64
    print("answer ran for ", n)
    return n * 10

function main()
    print("ul_3: ", ul_run(form: 3, cb: answer))
